docs/architecture.md:156:`tools/import-projectile-geometry.ts` recovers numerical sprite placements, shape/morph bounds, representative fill/line colors and line widths for34 projectile roots,53 sprites and79 leaves. It exports no vector paths or media. `assets/projectile-geometry.ts` composes those facts with retained poses, root rotation/scale, dynamic beam extents and turret facing. Script AABBs keep invisible helpers and declared morph start bounds, while visible procedural primitives exclude transparent helpers and honor animated morph ratios. Known empty frames stay empty; unknown future symbols retain a generic fallback.
docs/architecture.md:303:`simulation/actor-movement.ts` now owns active enemy/ally translation and delayed turn plans; `Tank.movement` replaces legacy steering counters. Registered behavior parts run after primary weapons and movement through `behaviors.ts`, consuming the separate destination, target-acquisition and Phasing modules. `ActorParents` owns simulation-only parent records: it distinguishes actor removal from unrooting an outgoing field wrapper and reparenting cached actors. It supplies parent-relative points without renderer objects or an active-only UID lookup. Parent records currently derive from World camera snapshots; per-assignment camera precision and matrix edge cases remain fidelity work. Healer retains its existing beam/patient owner until its overridden acquisition/Aim rules are recovered.
docs/architecture.md:306:`simulation/weapon-targets.ts` uses the same direct-reference target state as behaviors, separately for each offensive mount. Setup acquisition occurs during registered-part construction. The World parent tracker supplies attachment and cross-field projection; per-part Run/Aim acquisition and post-Aim ally-count refresh precede firing. `simulation/healer-target.ts` owns the distinct source Healer selector. Healing beams retain their own patient object. A known missing-ally read aborts the current World listener through a scoped error type while retained art and subsequent stage frames continue; unrelated JavaScript errors are not suppressed. The tank-wide target selector and field-wide target resets are removed.
docs/architecture.md:309:`core/weapon-aim.ts` records effective source manual/enemy aim flags at mount Setup. B1's first-primary gate can then disable the registered enemy primary rotation flags during movement. Rotating machine-gun and orbital Run overrides bypass the generic target/Aim prefix. Non-Healer behaviors invoke their inherited Aim between Run acquisition and post-Aim ally-count refresh, so Phasing retains its inherited rotation. `simulation/spikes.ts` owns seven-emitter geometric contact, reference-based contact memory and ordered force writes independently of firing timers. Known unparented/deactivated Spike reads join the scoped World listener boundary; arbitrary host errors still escape. Area Burst removes queried hostile destroyable shots immediately through the central removal path.
